( ── input-output leaves, batch A, 2026-08-29 evening ──

 'gen assert text equals' (a text compared against a literal expected
 value, no buffer-capture step) already exists in gen_things.vox
 (THG2-70) with this exact signature - reused here rather than copied,
 per 6a's "assertion helpers are generic" rule; grepped for before
 naming, per the 08-29 evening brief's own naming rule.)

(FMT-45, FMT-46, FMT-47, FMT-48, FMT-49: the escape table's five rows,
 each VERIFIED rather than merely printed — grep-confirmed absent before
 this leaf (buffers.md's byte-access idiom applied to the text side of
 the table for the first time). LANGUAGE.md:3573-3579. `{{`/`}}` render
 one literal brace each, `\n` a newline, `\t` a tab, `\\` one literal
 backslash — every one of the five decodes to exactly ONE byte, so with a
 P-byte prefix and an S-byte suffix (both plain letters/digits off 'gen
 buffer filler', so nothing here needs escaping of its own) the total
 size is always P+1+S and the escaped byte always sits at P+1: arithmetic
 the generator does at generation time, never read back at run time. A
 `text` has no size property (PROCEDURE.md 6a), so each escaped text is
 captured into a buffer declared straight from it (`gen_misc.vox`'s own
 "a buffer called X is Y" idiom) and read back by byte position.

 Two layers of escaping meet here, since this is a generator writing a
 generator's own escape test: to leave ONE literal `{`/`}` standing in
 the EMITTED program's string, `'open brace token'`/`'close brace
 token'` are written as their own STANDALONE Vox literals below
 (`"{{{{"`/`"}}}}"`, four characters each) — the same doubling
 `'gen leaf format types'`'s `'print escapes'` line already relies on,
 isolated here into its own name so the adjacent `{prefix}`/`{suffix}`
 slots never sit brace-to-brace with the escape token in one literal
 (which would leave the SCANNER — not just a human reader — guessing
 where the slot ends). `\n`/`\t`/`\\` follow the same two-hop shape with
 backslash doubling instead of brace doubling.

 FMT-50 (the escape table's own worked example) rides along at the end,
 emitted verbatim rather than asserted: it is three bare `Print`
 statements, and Print's own rendering has no in-program readback (see
 the report — same limit that leaves FMT-04/05/06 exercised only).

 Hand-verified against vox 0.4.14 and the 0.4.15 stack, byte for byte —
 docs/ledger/probes/input-output/FMT-45.vox, REPORT-LEAVES-FMT-A.md.)

